mes>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Camilli</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transcriptional regulation in the Streptococcus pneumoniae rlrA pathogenicity islet by RlrA</article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><year>2003</year><volume>185</volume><fpage>413</fpage><lpage>421</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12511486</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JB.185.2.413-421.2003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>LeMieux</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hava</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Basset</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Camilli</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>RrgA and RrgB are components of a multisubunit pilus encoded by the Streptococcus pneumoniae rlrA pathogenicity islet</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2006</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>2453</fpage><lpage>2456</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16552078</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/IAI.74.4.2453-2456.2006</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hemsley</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Joyce</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hava</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawale</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Camilli</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>MgrA, an orthologue of Mga, Acts as a transcriptional repressor of the genes within the rlrA pathogenicity islet in Streptococcus pneumoniae</article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><year>2003</year><volume>185</volume><fpage>6640</fpage><lpage>6647</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14594838</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JB.185.22.6640-6647.2003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gianfaldoni</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Censini</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hilleringmann</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Moschioni</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Facciotti</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pansegrau</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Masignani</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Covacci</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rappuoli</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Barocchi</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruggiero</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Streptococcus pneumoniae pilus subunits protect mice against lethal challenge</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2007</year><volume>75</volume><fpage>1059</fpage><lpage>1062</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17145945</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/IAI.01400-06</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tettelin</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Paulsen</surname><given-names>IT</given-names></name><name><surname>Eisen</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Read</surname><given-names>TD</given-names></name><name><surname>Peterson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Heidelberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>DeBoy</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Haft</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><name><surname>Dodson</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname